From: IT Support <postmaster@${DOMAIN_NAME}>
To: ${EMAIL}
Subject: Welcome! Corporate Mailbox Setup Guide, Storage Quota & Client Configuration
Date: ${DATE}
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Welcome to Your Corporate Mailbox</title>
</head>
<body style="font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333; max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px;">
  <div style="background-color: #2b6cb0; color: #ffffff; padding: 22px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 25px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: 22px;">Welcome! Your Corporate Email Account is Ready</h1>
    <p style="margin: 8px 0 0 0; opacity: 0.9;">Storage Quota, Desktop Client & Mobile App Setup Guide (Supports SMTP 587 / 465)</p>
  </div>

  <p>Dear <strong>${ACCOUNT}</strong>,</p>
  <p>Welcome to the team! Your corporate email account has been successfully initialized. Below are your storage quota policy, server connection parameters, and setup guides for desktop clients and mobile apps:</p>

  <!-- 1. Storage Quota Section -->
  <h3 style="color: #2b6cb0; border-bottom: 2px solid #edf2f7; padding-bottom: 8px;">📊 Storage Quota Information</h3>
  <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 25px; background-color: #f7fafc; border-radius: 6px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="padding: 10px 15px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0; font-weight: bold; width: 35%;">Allocated Mailbox Limit:</td>
      <td style="padding: 10px 15px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0; color: #2b6cb0; font-weight: bold; font-size: 16px;">${QUOTA_LIMIT} (Per System Configuration)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="padding: 10px 15px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0; font-weight: bold;">Warning & Over-Quota Policy:</td>
      <td style="padding: 10px 15px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;">
        • When storage reaches <strong>95%</strong>, an automated alert will be sent reminding you to clean up old or large emails.<br>
        • When storage reaches <strong>100%</strong> (full), the server will temporarily suspend receiving new incoming messages to protect data integrity.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background-color: #ebf8ff;">
      <td style="padding: 10px 15px; font-weight: bold; color: #2b6cb0;">Self-Service Status Query:</td>
      <td style="padding: 10px 15px; color: #2d3748;">
        Send an email to yourself with the subject <code style="background-color: #bee3f8; padding: 3px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: bold; color: #2b6cb0;">#status</code> or <code style="background-color: #bee3f8; padding: 3px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: bold; color: #2b6cb0;">#quota</code> anytime, and the system bot will reply within seconds with your real-time usage, percentage progress bar, and service status!
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <!-- 2. Server Connection Settings -->
  <h3 style="color: #2b6cb0; border-bottom: 2px solid #edf2f7; padding-bottom: 8px;">⚙️ Server Connection & Authentication Settings</h3>
  <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 25px;">
    <tr style="background-color: #f7fafc;">
      <td style="padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; font-weight: bold; width: 30%;">Configuration Item</td>
      <td style="padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; font-weight: bold;">Setting & Notes</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; font-weight: bold;">Email Address</td>
      <td style="padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;"><code style="color: #2b6cb0; font-weight: bold; font-size: 15px;">${EMAIL}</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background-color: #fffaf0;">
      <td style="padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #ecc94b; font-weight: bold; color: #b7791f;">Server Login Username</td>
      <td style="padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #ecc94b;">
        <code style="color: #c53030; font-weight: bold; font-size: 16px;">${ACCOUNT}</code>
        <div style="font-size: 13px; color: #c53030; margin-top: 4px; font-weight: bold;">
          ⚠️ Important: The login username is your pure account ID. DO NOT append "@${DOMAIN_NAME}"!
        </div>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; font-weight: bold;">Password</td>
      <td style="padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;">Your Windows Domain Password</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; font-weight: bold;">Incoming Server (IMAP)</td>
      <td style="padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;">Host <code>${HOST_NAME}</code> / Port <strong>993</strong> (SSL/TLS Encryption)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="background-color: #ebf8ff;">
      <td style="padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #bee3f8; font-weight: bold; color: #2b6cb0;">Outgoing Server (SMTP)</td>
      <td style="padding: 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #bee3f8;">
        • Server Host: <code>${HOST_NAME}</code><br>
        • Port Options (Both supported):<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;▸ <strong>Option 1: Port 587</strong> (Encryption: <strong>STARTTLS</strong> or TLS)<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;▸ <strong>Option 2: Port 465</strong> (Encryption: <strong>SSL/TLS</strong>)<br>
        • <strong style="color: #c53030;">Outgoing Authentication</strong>: <strong>Must check "My outgoing server (SMTP) requires authentication"</strong>, using pure account <code>${ACCOUNT}</code> (without @${DOMAIN_NAME}).
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <!-- 3. Desktop Client Setup Guide -->
  <h3 style="color: #2b6cb0; border-bottom: 2px solid #edf2f7; padding-bottom: 8px;">💻 Desktop Client Setup Guide (Outlook / Thunderbird / Mac Mail)</h3>
  <ol style="padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 25px; line-height: 1.8;">
    <li>Add a new account in your email client and choose <strong>"Manual setup or additional server types (IMAP)"</strong>.</li>
    <li>In Email Address enter <code>${EMAIL}</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>In Username, enter your pure account name <code>${ACCOUNT}</code> (DO NOT include @${DOMAIN_NAME})</strong>, and enter your domain password.</li>
    <li>Incoming Server (IMAP): <code>${HOST_NAME}</code>, Port: <strong>993</strong> (SSL/TLS).</li>
    <li>Outgoing Server (SMTP): <code>${HOST_NAME}</code>, Port: <strong>587 (STARTTLS)</strong> or <strong>465 (SSL/TLS)</strong>.</li>
    <li>Go to the "Outgoing Server" tab and <strong>check "My outgoing server (SMTP) requires authentication"</strong> (use same settings as incoming).</li>
  </ol>

  <!-- 4. Mobile App Setup & Auth Error Guide -->
  <div style="background-color: #fffaf0; border-left: 4px solid #dd6b20; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 25px;">
    <h4 style="margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #c05621; font-size: 16px;">📱 Mobile App Initial Setup Guide (iOS / Android / Outlook Mobile)</h4>
    <p style="margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-size: 14px; color: #7b341e;">
      <strong>⚠️ Why does initial mobile setup show "Authentication Failed / Invalid Credentials"?</strong><br>
      When adding an account on mobile, the app initially prompts for your full email (<code>${EMAIL}</code>) and password. When testing connection, the app attempts to log in using the full email as the username. Because company servers require pure account authentication, <strong>this initial attempt will always fail. This is normal and expected!</strong>
    </p>
    <div style="font-size: 14px; color: #2d3748; line-height: 1.8;">
      <strong>Quick Fix:</strong>
      <ol style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>Tap <strong>"Manual Setup" or "Advanced Settings"</strong> on your phone.</li>
        <li>In the <strong>Username</strong> field (for both Incoming and Outgoing servers), <strong>delete the auto-filled "@{DOMAIN_NAME}" to leave only your pure account name <code><span style="color: #c53030; font-weight: bold;">${ACCOUNT}</span></code></strong>!</li>
        <li>Set Outgoing Server Port to <strong>587 (STARTTLS)</strong> or <strong>465 (SSL/TLS)</strong>, and ensure <strong>"Server Requires Authentication"</strong> is turned ON.</li>
        <li>Tap Save / Sign In to complete the setup and start emailing!</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  <!-- 5. SSL/TLS Certificate Warning Guidance -->
  <div style="background-color: #f7fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 25px;">
    <h4 style="margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #2b6cb0; font-size: 16px;">🔒 SSL/TLS Security Certificate Warning & Self-Signed Certificate Guide</h4>
    <p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 13px; color: #4a5568;">
      If this mail server uses an internal or self-signed certificate, your email software or mobile app may display a "Security Alert" or "Untrusted Certificate" warning upon initial connection. Please follow the instructions below to trust/bypass and continue:
    </p>
    <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; font-size: 13px; color: #2d3748; line-height: 1.8;">
      <li><strong>Microsoft Outlook (Desktop):</strong> When the security warning window appears ("Cannot verify certificate"), simply click <strong>"Yes"</strong> to continue using this server.</li>
      <li><strong>Mozilla Thunderbird:</strong> When the security exception window appears, check "Permanently store this exception" and click <strong>"Confirm Security Exception"</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Apple iPhone / iPad (iOS Mail):</strong> When the <strong>"Cannot Verify Server Identity"</strong> pop-up appears, tap <strong>"Continue"</strong> to proceed (or tap "Details" and tap "Trust" in the top right).</li>
      <li><strong>Android Devices (Gmail / Samsung Mail / Outlook Mobile):</strong> If an untrusted certificate warning appears, tap <strong>"Advanced" ➔ "Continue anyway"</strong>; or in the security type menu, select an option with <strong>"Accept all certificates"</strong> (e.g., SSL/TLS accept all).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; margin: 25px 0 15px 0;">
  <p style="font-size: 12px; color: #718096; margin: 0;">IT Infrastructure Team | System Generated Notification - Please do not reply directly to this email</p>
</body>
</html>
